// The standard library module wasm (card warp-host-wasm-load, notes/warp_host.md): `use wasm`, other WebAssembly
// modules and components loaded into the running program, through the adapter std_io. warp-host serves it; the browser
// and warp-rust don't yet.
// `m = load_wasm("lib.wasm")`: a core module (instantiated beside the program, with the same imports) or a component
// (by its header, WIT types), its handle {wasm: 1, path: "lib.wasm", kind: "module"}; a path is loaded once per run,
// bytes (read_bytes, compile_wasm) each time anew
load_wasm(module: any) := std_io("wasm", "load", [module])
// `wasm_call(m, "twice", [21])`: an export called, the arguments as its types want them, its result a warp value;
// m may be a handle or a path. Numbers cross as numbers, a component's strings, lists, records, options, results and
// enums by its WIT types; a trap or a result's err is an Error
wasm_call(module: any, name: any, arguments: any) := std_io("wasm", "call", [module, name, arguments])
// `wasm_exports(m)`: each export's name and type, {twice: "func(i64) -> i64"}
wasm_exports(module: any) := std_io("wasm", "exports", [module])
